    "summary": "High‑energy Wichita set with soaring Bird Song and tight Truckin’→The Other One",
    "blurb": "The show bursts with a smoking Bird Song and a flawless Truckin' → The Other One transition. Jerry’s leads are scorching, Keith’s piano jazzy, and the rhythm section stays locked in throughout. Both soundboard sources capture the performance with excellent clarity.",
    "review": "November 17, 1972 at Century II Convention Hall finds the Dead firing on all cylinders. The first set rolls from a crisp rendition of The Promised Land into a soaring Bird Song that showcases Garcia’s beautiful, almost scorching tone, while Phil’s bass sings alongside Bob’s confident rhythm work. A highlight is the seamless Truckin' → The Other One jam in the second set – Keith Godchaux’s jazzy piano weaves through the improvisation, and Bill Kreutzmann (Billy) drives the groove with unstoppable energy. The night closes on a mellow Brokedown Palace that feels like a gentle exhale after the high‑octane explorations, making this Wichita gig one of the standout performances of the 1972 tour.",
